onial / Customer Review, Storytelling, Greenscreen, Tutorial, Social Proof Mashup, Reaction Video, Unboxing, Listicle, POV, Styling Reel, Trend, ASMR, Street Interview, Podcast, Comment Response\n\nANGLE:\nIdentify whether the video's primary emotional driver is Pain (leads with a problem the viewer has) or Desire (leads with an outcome the viewer wants).\n\nSTAGE:\nIdentify the funnel stage: TOF (interrupts cold audiences with a problem or pattern interrupt), MOF (assumes some awareness, focuses on solution and benefits), BOF (speaks to buyers ready to convert using proof and urgency).\n\n---\n\nHOOK FRAME RULES:\nThe first frame in the storyboard is always the Hook. For this frame the fields work as follows:\n- voiceover: [Hook type name] - [1-2 sentences explaining why this hook type was chosen and what it achieves for the viewer]. This is the educational layer.\n- caption: The actual on-screen TEXT OVERLAY copy visible in this frame. None if no caption exists in the video.\n- caption_detail: [Caption hook type name] - [1-2 sentences explaining why this caption type works here and what job it does on screen]. None if no caption.\n- visual_action: Description of what the creator physically does or shows in the opening frame.\n- visual_action_detail: [Visual action hook type name] - [1-2 sentences explaining why this visual action was chosen and what it signals to the viewer].\n\nExample voiceover: \"Relatability - this hook works because it positions the creator as someone who had the same doubts as the viewer, making them feel understood before the product is even mentioned.\"\n\nFor every subsequent frame:\n- voiceover: Explanation of what the audio or delivery achieves in this frame, or None if the creator is not speaking and there is no voiceover.\n- caption: Actual on-screen TEXT OVERLAY copy, or None. NEVER closed captions or subtitles.\n- caption_detail: Explanation of why this caption was placed here and what it adds. None if no caption.\n- visual_action: 